# A Polish vowel is not much shorter unstressed than stressed, where Italian's
# is less than half: Italian starts a vowel's length from a share of its
# inherent length, a hundred or more when the syllable is stressed and 45 to
# 55 when it is not, and the unstressed u of Mateusz and nauczyciel came out
# at 51 and 45 ms against 126 for the stressed e beside it. So the share
# Italian picks, in variable 2628, is raised to a floor; a stressed vowel's is
# above it already and barely moves. The floor is the ear's, chosen from 65
# to 200 at the ordinary rate and at 400 words a minute; above about 120 it
# lengthens the stressed vowels as well. Nothing Italian adjusts afterwards is
# where the shortening was: each of those five, left out in turn, still gave
# the same u.
rule pol_stanital_start_dur takes 3 from is_sidur.obj
  afresh
  variable share word 2628
  call assign_stanital_start_dur arg 1 arg 2
  if answer is not 0
    give up
  end
  if share is less than 105
    set share to 105
  end
  match
end
